400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 210 0 R
/E (People rarely remember the exact name or exact words of a file they saved months ago. They remember a topic, a few words, a rough time, or the look of a page. Ordinary file- name search and plain keyword search both fail in that situation, and cloud-based assistants solve it only by uploading private documents to a remote service.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 210 0 R
/E (This project presents AFTERIMAGE, a local-first document retrieval system that finds a stored document from an imperfect fragment of memory. The core engine is written in C++20 and is built as eight cooperating modules: document model, folder ingestion, content extraction \(plain text, Markdown, PDF text, scanned PDF and image OCR through Poppler and Tesseract\), SQLite persistence, a positional inverted index, a fragment retrieval engine, a ranking engine and a document-concept memory graph. Retrieval combines five routes: exact, prefix \(ordered-map range search\), infix \(middle-of-word\), typo-tolerant \(bounded Levenshtein distance\) and phrase \(position-based\). Candidates are ranked with the BM25 model multiplied by a per-route reliability factor, plus explicit title, path, phrase, coverage and recency boosts, so every result carries a score breakdown. A breadth-first search over the concept graph then suggests related documents.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
