502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 214 0 R
/E (The work was divided into the tasks below, which also define the framework of this report.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 214 0 R
/E (A person wants to open a document they saved earlier but can recall it only as a fragment: a few letters of a word, a spelling that is slightly wrong, a phrase from inside the text, a topic, a rough time, or the type of file. Searching by file name fails because the name is forgotten. Searching by exact keyword fails because the typed word is wrong, partial or different from the word in the file. Text that exists only inside scanned pages and images cannot be searched at all. Finally, a flat list of matches does not tell the person why a file matched, where inside it to look, or which other files are related.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 214 0 R
/E (The client for this project is an individual student or professional who keeps a large personal library of study notes, source files, PDFs, scanned pages and screenshots on a local computer. Digital storage is cheap, so such libraries keep growing, but the time to find one specific file does not shrink. The contemporary issue is that most people can no longer find their own information by its name or exact keyword, and the usual cure, a cloud AI assistant, requires uploading private documents to a remote service.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 214 0 R
/E (The need was justified in three ways. No external statistical survey was conducted, so no survey figures are claimed.)
