/T (The web layer adds the columns tags, user_notes, extraction_method, page_count and indexed_at_epoch_seconds, and a second table semantic_vectors \(document_id, content_hash, dimensions, vector BLOB, indexed_at\). Implementation points: a RAII class Statement prepares a statement in its constructor and finalises it in its destructor, so a thrown error cannot leak a prepared statement; all values are passed through bound parameters \(sqlite3_bind_*\) and never pasted into SQL; documents are saved with INSERT ... ON CONFLICT\(id\) DO UPDATE; saveAll runs BEGIN IMMEDIATE, saves every document and COMMITs, and ROLLBACKs on any exception; a busy timeout of 5)
/E (The web layer adds the columns tags, user_notes, extraction_method, page_count and indexed_at_epoch_seconds, and a second table semantic_vectors \(document_id, content_hash, dimensions, vector BLOB, indexed_at\). Implementation points: a RAII class Statement prepares a statement in its constructor and finalises it in its destructor, so a thrown error cannot leak a prepared statement; all values are passed through bound parameters \(sqlite3_bind_*\) and never pasted into SQL; documents are saved with INSERT ... ON CONFLICT\(id\) DO UPDATE; saveAll runs BEGIN IMMEDIATE, saves every document and COMMITs, and ROLLBACKs on any exception; a busy timeout of 5)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
