/T (Security and robustness. Shell injection is avoided by launching tools with argument arrays; hanging tools are stopped by a 120 s timeout, output cap and SIGKILL; memory use is bounded by size limits; symbolic links are never followed; the database is protected by transactions and bound parameters; the server listens on 127.0.0.1 only; and every file is processed inside its own try/catch.)
/E (Security and robustness. Shell injection is avoided by launching tools with argument arrays; hanging tools are stopped by a 120 s timeout, output cap and SIGKILL; memory use is bounded by size limits; symbolic links are never followed; the database is protected by transactions and bound parameters; the server listens on 127.0.0.1 only; and every file is processed inside its own try/catch.)
