/T (Web adapter. A standard-library HTTP server bound to 127.0.0.1:8765 calls the C++ binary with argument lists, so the engine remains the single implementation of search. Its endpoints are listed in Table 3.9. A BackgroundIndexer runs the engine in a worker thread, streams output into a lock-protected log, supports cancellation and afterwards labels each document with its extraction method and an estimated page count.)
